# Hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) backend in SITL: --model hil (real time) or
# hil:lockstep (libraries/SITL/examples/HIL/readme.md). SITL's SERIAL5 is
# a TCP port (5765 + 10 x instance; --serial5 moves it) that carries the
# link to the simulator bridge, e.g. Tools/autotest/pysim/hil_bridge.py
SERIAL5_PROTOCOL 100
# the 200 Hz main loop the HIL link is sized for, and the reference
# bridge's default --loop-rate-hz; Rover's own default is 50 Hz
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 200
# HIL log records also before arming
LOG_DISARMED 1
